2026/11/26 15:14:43 workflow_v2_integration.go:4464: [workflow-v2-template] Coding Agent Event: {"version":1,"agent":"coding","event":"tool_started","phase":"running","task_id":"T1","title":"继续","ts":"2026-11-26T07:14:43.78763Z","detail":"ssh","command":"cd /root/qm26work/qmobjdetv26 \u0026\u0026 python3 - \u003c\u003c'PY'\nimport io\np='docs/mips-performance.md'\ns=io.open(p,encoding='utf-8').read()\nold='''**T16 changes that statement once, and only behind a knob.** One source change\n(stride-2 triple fusion, §6a) was adopted and A/B'd at **-8.06%**, but it ships\nwith `QM26_FUSE_S2` defaulting to **off**, because enabling it deletes eight\nintermediates from the tensor set and therefore re-baselines the 110-line blob\ndump. Everything else in T16 was rejected and is recorded in §6 and §6a, so the\ndefault binary still produces the §5 numbers.'''\nnew='''**T16 changed that statement once, behind a knob; T18 turned the knob on.** One\nsource change (stride-2 triple fusion, §6a) was adopted and A/B'd at **-8.06%**\nin T16, but shipped with `QM26_FUSE_S2` defaulting to **off**, because enabling\nit deletes eight intermediates from the tensor set and therefore re-baselines the\n110-line blob dump. **T18 made it the default** after re-baselining that fixture\n(102 lines) and re-verifying the numbers: the 102 surviving blobs are\nbyte-identical, the detection fingerprint is unchanged, and a paired A/B on the\nshipping binary measured **-5.7%** frame time (CI95 [-6.5,-4.2]). Everything else\nin T16 was rejected and is recorded in §6 and §6a. The §5 numbers below predate\nT18 and are quoted for provenance, not as the current default.'''\nassert s.count(old)==1\ns=s.replace(old,new)\nio.open(p,'w',encoding='utf-8',newline='').write(s)\nprint('ok')\nPY\nsed -n '15,28p' docs/mips-performance.md"}
